[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Example problems from contests such as USAMO, USA TSTST, CMO, IMO, or the IMO Shortlist, with contest and year cited",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Complete, correct, logically justified solutions rather than answer sketches",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Post-solution insights, reusable takeaways, and discussion of tempting but unsuccessful approaches",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "A coherent series structure with prerequisites, progression, and clear post-level titles"
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       ]
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]     },
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]     {
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       "name": "Pigeonhole, invariants, and extremal methods",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       "brief": "Create a complementary sequence of blog posts on pigeonhole and averaging arguments, invariants and monovariants, extremal principle, coloring, and finite-process or game arguments. Emphasize how contestants discover the right objects, states, or extremal choices. Use authentic high-level olympiad examples, giving exact statements and independently checked solutions.",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       "must_cover": [
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Accessible intuition plus detailed formal explanations of pigeonhole, invariants, monovariants, coloring, and extremal choices",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Conditions and limitations of each method, including how to choose useful holes, quantities, colorings, or extremal objects",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Representative examples from USAMO, USA TSTST, CMO, IMO, IMO Shortlist, or comparable top olympiads, identified by source and year",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Fully correct step-by-step solutions covering edge cases and equality or termination issues where relevant",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Explicit insights, recognition cues, generalizations, and takeaways after every example",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Posts organized as a progressively challenging olympiad-training series"
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       ]
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]     },
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]     {
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       "name": "Graphs, set systems, and advanced constructions",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       "brief": "Write the advanced portion of the blog series on graph-theoretic reformulation, degree and path arguments, matchings, tournaments, set systems, permutations, constructive combinatorics, and probabilistic arguments when olympiad-appropriate. Explain both the underlying structures and how to translate an unfamiliar problem into them. Ground the posts in verified problems from leading olympiads.",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       "must_cover": [
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Intuitive and rigorous treatment of graph models, degree counting, connectivity, paths and cycles, matchings, tournaments, set systems, and constructive methods",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Careful inclusion of probabilistic or advanced techniques only where they are relevant and explainable at olympiad level",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Authentic example problems from USAMO, USA TSTST, CMO, IMO, IMO Shortlist, and similar top contests, with accurate attribution",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Complete and correct solutions, including construction verification, bounds, and extremal or equality cases",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "For each solution, the key translation or breakthrough, transferable lessons, alternative viewpoints where useful, and common pitfalls",
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]         "Self-contained blog-post presentation that fits with the foundational and intermediate posts while avoiding unnecessary duplication"
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]       ]
[6847465956a0f6376a6054be:parallel_evidence]     }
