[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]     {
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "name": "LSTM history and applications",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "brief": "Develop the LSTM portion of a comprehensive seminar-paper outline, tracing the architecture from the recurrent-network vanishing-gradient problem through Hochreiter and Schmidhuber’s original work and subsequent technical milestones. Explain mechanisms accessibly but precisely, distinguish LSTMs from generic RNNs and from encoder-decoder systems that may use LSTM cells, and document practical and societal consequences. Identify five non-overlapping case studies for later cross-case synthesis, supported by peer-reviewed literature or credible historical accounts.",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "must_cover": [
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Origins of recurrent neural networks and the vanishing/exploding-gradient problem, including why long-range dependencies were difficult to learn",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Hochreiter and Schmidhuber’s contribution and the LSTM cell’s gates, memory state, gradient flow, and training mechanism",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Major later milestones and variants, such as forget gates, bidirectionality, stacked LSTMs, and relevant training or hardware advances",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Historical adoption, limitations, alternatives, and changing role after attention and transformers",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Five clearly bounded case studies collectively illustrating areas such as speech recognition, predictive text, language modeling, translation, or other sequence tasks",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Documented effects on practicality, performance, accessibility, globalization, labor, and deployment risks where relevant to the five cases",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Peer-reviewed technical sources and credible historical accounts for every substantive claim, with quantitative evidence where available"
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       ]
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]     },
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]     {
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "name": "Encoder-decoder evolution",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "brief": "Develop the encoder-decoder/seq2seq portion of the outline as a distinct but intersecting architectural history. Trace its conceptual origins and landmark work by Cho, Sutskever, Bahdanau, and collaborators through attention, large-scale neural machine translation, and modern encoder-decoder transformers. Explain how the architecture works, where LSTMs fit within it, and whether or in what sense encoder-decoder models dominate present-day NLP. Supply five additional, non-overlapping case studies with rigorous evidence.",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "must_cover": [
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Prehistory and origins of neural encoder-decoder and sequence-to-sequence modeling, including the contributions and chronology of Cho, Sutskever, and collaborators",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Fixed-vector encoding, decoding, teacher forcing, inference, bottlenecks, and other core technical mechanisms and limitations",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Bahdanau-style attention, its motivation and effects, followed by the transition to transformer encoder-decoder models",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Milestones in neural machine translation and expansion into speech, summarization, dialogue, and other sequence-to-sequence tasks",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Present-day status across NLP, carefully distinguishing encoder-only, decoder-only, recurrent seq2seq, and transformer encoder-decoder systems rather than assuming universal dominance",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Five clearly bounded case studies, non-overlapping with the LSTM cases, that provide quantitative and historical evidence of technical adoption and social consequences",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Peer-reviewed literature and credible historical accounts supporting all technical, chronological, and impact claims"
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       ]
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]     },
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]     {
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "name": "Comparison, ethics, and synthesis",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "brief": "Create the integrative section and overall synthesis framework for the paper. Directly compare LSTMs with encoder-decoder architectures historically, technically, and socially, while emphasizing that they are not mutually exclusive categories. Synthesize the ten case studies gathered across the other facets into broader, evidence-bounded conclusions about responsible technology and possible strategies for ethical innovation. Analyze benefits, distributional effects, and harms using formal ethical and governance frameworks, including relevant IEEE guidance, without treating aspirational principles as proof of outcomes.",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       "must_cover": [
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Direct historical comparison of origins, milestone timelines, adoption patterns, decline or persistence, and influence on later AI architectures",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Direct technical comparison of architectural level, memory and context handling, training, inference, scalability, strengths, limitations, and the possibility of LSTM-based encoder-decoders",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Comparative societal impacts on machine translation, speech recognition, predictive text, globalization, accessibility, and jobs, including who benefits and who bears costs",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Ethical analysis of training-data bias, unequal access, linguistic and disability inclusion, labor displacement or transformation, privacy, surveillance, and disinformation misuse",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Cross-case synthesis of exactly ten case studies from the two architecture facets, identifying recurring mechanisms, contextual differences, tradeoffs, and limits on generalization",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Responsible-technology conclusions and feasible ethical-innovation strategies involving evaluation, data governance, transparency, human oversight, access, accountability, and misuse safeguards",
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]         "Use of peer-reviewed evidence, historical accounts, and formal ethical frameworks such as applicable IEEE guidelines, with clear separation of empirical findings, ethical judgments, and recommendations"
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]       ]
[6847465956a0f6376a605360:parallel_evidence]     }
